  "limitations": [
    "Authored AOT fixtures execute no game bytes. No new game object or startup execution coverage is claimed.",
    "AMD conditional pointer and selector behavior is an explicit manual-based policy tested alongside Intel hardware results, not an AMD hardware observation.",
    "Hardware comparisons use 32-bit last-pointer values to avoid the independently documented host upper-pointer preservation limit. The pure serializer repeats retain separate full-width checks and counted host-loss classification.",
